Done. Here's a summary of what was implemented:

**Created `public/js/ping.ts`** — Canvas overlay module. Renders expanding rings in screen-pixel-equivalent sizes (divided by viewport scale), with white shadow/glow for visibility on dark fog, and a brief fill flash at impact. Rings fade over 3 seconds using `requestAnimationFrame`.

**Modified `src/ws/messages.ts`** — Added `PingMapMessage` (client→server) and `PingMapBroadcast` (server→client) types to their respective unions.

**Modified `src/ws/handler.ts`** — Added `ping:map` case: attaches sender name ("GM" or player name), broadcasts back to sender + all clients in the adventure topic. No persistence.

**Modified `public/js/gm.ts`** — Ping layer initialized between canvas and token layer (correct z-order). Long-press: 100ms viewport grace + 400ms timer = 500ms total. Cancels if pointer moves >5px. Suppresses fog drawing while pinging. Rate-limited to 1/sec. GM ping color: `#4a4aff`.

**Modified `public/js/player.ts`** — Same long-press pattern. Tracks own token position (`ownTokenPos`) to skip long-press when pressing on own token. Player ping color: their chosen color. Pings cleared on map switch.
